  "content": {
    "title": "Is Easter a federal holiday? Are banks, post offices open? What to know",
    "text": "April 3, 2026, 11:51 a.m. ETEaster, a Christian holiday commemorating the resurrection of Jesus Christ, is Sunday.But is the religious observance recognized as a federal holiday in the United States? Will essential services, like mail delivery, be operating as usual?Here's what to know.Is Easter a federal holiday?No, Good Friday, Easter Sunday and Easter Monday are not among the 12 federal holidays recognized in 2026. Christmas Day is the only religious federal holiday in the United States.Are banks open on Easter Sunday?Some national banks, including Bank of America, Wells Fargo, PNC, Truist, and CitiBank, may close on Easter as these banks typically do not operate on Sundays.Is USPS post office open on Easter Sunday?According to Newsweek, USPS post offices will be closed on Easter Sunday. Regular mail delivery will also not be operating. However, the site adds that Priority Mail Express will still be available for \"urgent shipments.\"Is FedEx open on Easter Sunday?FedEx will be closed on Easter Sunday, per Newsweek. Most shipping and pickup services will be suspended on April 5, but the company's normal operations are expected to resume on Monday, April 6.Is UPS open today on Easter Sunday?UPS will also be closed on Easter Sunday.Is the stock market open on Easter Sunday?The stock markets on New York Stock Exchange and the Nasdaq are closed for trading on Good Friday, April 3, 2026. The Securities Industry and Financial Markets Association also recommended an early close at noon EST for the holiday.Is the stock market open on Easter Sunday?All stock markets, including the Nasdaq, New York Stock Exchange and U.S. bond market, will be closed on Sunday, April 5, and will reopen Monday, April 6.",
